The textbook she was currently using wasn't particularly\nhigh-level.%K%P
现在她使用的参考书水平并不高。%K%P
I had already realized that it would probably be no good\nto us if we were seriously looking to earn a scholarship\nfrom a school like Shuusen.%K%P
想要考取秋泉大附属的免费生，那书完全不够用，\n在教她英语的时候我深刻感受到了这一点。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dIt's well-written, and the explanations are quite\ndetailed. It also has a lot of examples, so it's easy to\nunderstand. It was my favorite textbook back in school.\d%K%P
「阅读简单，解释详细，例文很多，\n至少在我用过的参考书里，这个是最棒的了」%K%P
It was the last copy the shop had, relegated to a corner\naway from all the newer, flashier stuff they were trying\nto sell.%K%P
书架的角落里，静静地躺着那仅有的一本参考书。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\d...I'm sorry for picking such a boring present.\d%K%P
「…抱歉，这个礼物很无聊」%K%P
I will not forget Himeo's broad smile the moment she found\nthat copy for as long as I live.%K%P
看到书背面封皮的时候，姫绪小姐的脸上，\n露出的尴尬微笑，我没有看漏。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
